{"status":"completed","summary":"The staged help site is served by nginx on TCP 8080. `/manual/` URLs permanently redirect to corresponding `/help/` paths with query strings preserved, while `/status.txt` returns the supplied document directly. Configuration, firewall, and SELinux policy survived the required node reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed the RHEL-supported nginx 1.26.3 package.","Configured `/etc/nginx/conf.d/help-site.conf` for the staged content and HTTP 301 redirects.","Enabled persistent SELinux labels and TCP 8080 policy while retaining enforcing mode.","Opened TCP 8080 in runtime and permanent firewalld configuration.","Enabled nginx at boot and removed the packaged port-80 listener.","Retained a root-only rollback copy at `/etc/nginx/nginx.conf.pre-help-site`.","Safely rebooted node1 and verified complete recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Serve the staged help tree on TCP 8080","command_ids":["cmd-663a9dc9bb634d6b","cmd-c1a647e832874376"],"summary":"Help pages return HTTP 200 with source-matching content; nginx is active, enabled, and listening on IPv4/IPv6 port 8080."},{"requirement":"Permanently redirect manual URLs while preserving path and query string","command_ids":["cmd-663a9dc9bb634d6b","cmd-c1a647e832874376"],"summary":"Nested `/manual/network/setup.html` requests return HTTP 301 to `/help/network/setup.html` with all query parameters retained, before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Keep `/status.txt` available without redirect","command_ids":["cmd-663a9dc9bb634d6b","cmd-c1a647e832874376"],"summary":"The endpoint returns HTTP 200 directly, and its served SHA-256 hash matches the supplied status document."},{"requirement":"Preserve the installed OS release, kernel, and security controls","command_ids":["cmd-3fcdc8f257ca404e","cmd-c1a647e832874376"],"summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 remain installed; SELinux remains enforcing."},{"requirement":"Persistent firewall and SELinux configuration","command_ids":["cmd-5b0a50d64e894623","cmd-c1a647e832874376"],"summary":"The content has persistent `httpd_sys_content_t` labeling and TCP 8080 remains permitted by both runtime and permanent firewall configuration after reboot."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-e7cc818a33584de0","cmd-f1d66a5de3da4ed8","cmd-cd2163f99d8c4c5e","cmd-c1a647e832874376"],"summary":"Healthy baseline was captured, safe reboot acknowledged, boot ID changed from `d49beed9-f2bc-4611-892b-e25e35071bc5` to `60ee60eb-290b-466f-8a86-f95894d6620b`, and service, content, redirect, firewall, and SELinux recovery were directly verified."}]}
